{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus","id":928258,"title":"Solar Brawler is transformed into a Stegosaurus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-08T10:47:05-07:00","id":928258,"title":"Solar Brawler is transformed into a Stegosaurus","content":"<b>Siege Lizard, page 572</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attack (Tail Slam): 7 dice (Damage 19, minimum 5). The siege lizard\u2019s tail can be used to make smashing attacks.<br /> <br /> Spiked Tail Slam: When the siege lizard makes a smashing decisive tail slam attack while at Initiative 12+, that attack gains the benefits of Heaven Thunder Hammer (see p. 274). </div> </div> </div>What happens when the Solar enhances this Brawl attack with the <i>actual</i> Heaven Thunder Hammer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:51:39-07:00","id":928260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus#post928258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Siege Lizard, page 572</b><br /> <br /> <br /> What happens when the Solar enhances this Brawl attack with the <i>actual</i> Heaven Thunder Hammer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with nothing, personally. You already have the effects of the charm, and it's not stackable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:57:21-07:00","id":928272,"title":"","content":"That is not how Charms work. They are either explicitly inapplicable, as in the case of attempting to use HTH with a Melee weapon, or else they enhance an action.<br /> <br /> If you have a Charm that lets you count a Melee attack as a smashing attack regardless of the weapon's actual abilities, and you use that Charm with a weapon which can execute smashing attacks on its own, the Charm should grant a more effective smashing attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:04:40-07:00","id":928279,"title":"","content":"Nothing. A mere spiky tail cannot bear the might of your true glory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:06:55-07:00","id":928280,"title":"","content":"I would agree with the nothing. The Charm is not Stackable, therefore multiple applications of the Charm, from whatever source, would not stack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:19:31-07:00","id":928289,"title":"","content":"Do Solars get to use their charms in forms other than humanish? Whatever your group's answer to this question is will answer your OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:23:04-07:00","id":928294,"title":"","content":"No stack\u2026 but you knew I'd say that already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:25:50-07:00","id":928296,"title":"","content":"Nothing. This is using compartmentalized systemic logic first and other logic second. I know the book is over 1/2 rules, but using systemic logic first only makes those rules worse, not better. How you feel about that is a different issue entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:57:58-07:00","id":928358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928280#post928280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree with the nothing. The Charm is not Stackable, therefore multiple applications of the Charm, from whatever source, would not stack.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lack of a Stackable keyword only concerns the Charm itself. The Charm cannot be activated twice.<br /> <br /> The tail is not a Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:59:38-07:00","id":928361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928358#post928358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of a Stackable keyword only concerns the Charm itself. The Charm cannot be activated twice.<br /> <br /> The tail is not a Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew you wouldn't care for my answer, but there it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:59:45-07:00","id":928362,"title":"","content":"I'm more curious to see this ability interact with lunar charms to be quite honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:06:59-07:00","id":928366,"title":"","content":"This is, frankly, kind of a ridiculous edge case so unlikely that it should probably be resolved on a table-to-table basis.<br /> <br /> IMHO, I'd say that if you have HTH using this tail slam probably counts as a free activation of it for the purpose of itself or any charms that might stem from it. But I wouldn't let you stack it on top of the extant tail slam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:07:09-07:00","id":928367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928362#post928362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more curious to see this ability interact with lunar charms to be quite honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the reason I was thinking about this. The largest reason why Lunars cannot have a version of HTH as strong as the Solar one is the possibility that its effects would stack too well with natural animal attacks like these. So the question is how much they stack at all.<br /> <br /> Which then turned out to be a disagreement about WHETHER they stack at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:09:14-07:00","id":928369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928367#post928367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the reason I was thinking about this. The largest reason why Lunars cannot have a version of HTH as strong as the Solar one is the possibility that its effects would stack too well with natural animal attacks like these. So the question is how much they stack at all.<br /> <br /> Which then turned out to be a disagreement about WHETHER they stack at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that's actually a pretty solid question. OTOH, IIRC animal attacks were constructed kind of like the Eclipse keyword--&quot;Lunars will have access to this&quot; was a definite consideration.<br /> <br /> So hopefully there will be an answer in the pages of the Lunar book when it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:54:18-07:00","id":928402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928369#post928369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's actually a pretty solid question. OTOH, IIRC animal attacks were constructed kind of like the Eclipse keyword--&quot;Lunars will have access to this&quot; was a definite consideration.<br /> <br /> So hopefully there will be an answer in the pages of the Lunar book when it happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am attempting to homebrew Lunar Charms, and Count Alucard believes that the stegosaurus' mighty tail attack cannot be supplemented by a Lunar Strength Charm which would cause knockback with normal attacks / smashing attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:30:54-07:00","id":928429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928402#post928402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am attempting to homebrew Lunar Charms, and Count Alucard believes that the stegosaurus' mighty tail attack cannot be supplemented by a Lunar Strength Charm which would cause knockback with normal attacks / smashing attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably should've contextualized it as that instead of trying to make a case via rules legalism without context, because the latter has no real oomph to it. That changes the issue quite a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:47:41-07:00","id":928450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928402#post928402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am attempting to homebrew Lunar Charms, and Count Alucard believes that the stegosaurus' mighty tail attack cannot be supplemented by a Lunar Strength Charm which would cause knockback with normal attacks / smashing attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The clear advantage of the Lunar charm would be that it doesn't require the buildup of Initiative, so it's not wholly redundant. If the Lunar charm has further benefits outside of knockback, it may have its cost discounted. If not...I dunno. I might add some sort of bonus to the knockback, like treating the HTH Tail Slam as though it had its Essence 3 upgrade, esp. if the Lunar Charm doesn't upgrade in the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:59:45-07:00","id":928482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928402#post928402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am attempting to homebrew Lunar Charms, and Count Alucard believes that the stegosaurus' mighty tail attack cannot be supplemented by a Lunar Strength Charm which would cause knockback with normal attacks / smashing attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>then why are you asking so vaguely about solar charms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T16:07:19-07:00","id":928486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928482#post928482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then why are you asking so vaguely about solar charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Count Alucard and I were having a disagreement about what SHOULD happen when a normal ability and a Charm with the same effect are used together. He thought nothing should happen, and I thought that something more should happen.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, he thought that nothing should be able to improve upon an effect like Heaven Thunder Hammer, even if it was a Celestial Exalt putting their magic behind it.<br /> <br /> <br /> This seemed like the best example to offer, since it uses officially printed material.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928429#post928429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably should've contextualized it as that instead of trying to make a case via rules legalism without context, because the latter has no real oomph to it. That changes the issue quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I created the thread on lunch-break with my iPad. I <i>might</i> not have thought it through enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928450#post928450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might add some sort of bonus to the knockback, like treating the HTH Tail Slam as though it had its Essence 3 upgrade, esp. if the Lunar Charm doesn't upgrade in the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thanks. I'd forgotten about that clause. Probably because I'm trying to read the rules from my phone or pad.<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-08-2016, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T16:19:08-07:00","id":928491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928486#post928486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Count Alucard and I were having a disagreement about what SHOULD happen when a normal ability and a Charm with the same effect are used together. He thought nothing should happen, and I thought that something more should happen.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, he thought that nothing should be able to improve upon an effect like Heaven Thunder Hammer, even if it was a Celestial Exalt putting their magic behind it.<br /> <br /> <br /> This seemed like the best example to offer, since it uses officially printed material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you seem to have decided that something ought to, since you're asking &quot;what happens&quot; and not taking &quot;nothing&quot; for an answer when it is a perfectly valid one. Plus &quot;What if X?&quot; is a very different question than &quot;What if X, if X is actually Y?&quot;, where Y is something you kinda need to make up on your own from the start. We're in &quot;make shit up&quot; territory. so make shit up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T16:47:53-07:00","id":928503,"title":"","content":"They gain the Essence 3+ effect regardless of whether they're Essence 3+ or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11872-lessens","name":"lessens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T18:06:46-07:00","id":928539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lessens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928503#post928503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They gain the Essence 3+ effect regardless of whether they're Essence 3+ or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if they ARE 3+, they probably gain the 7+ effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T19:03:35-07:00","id":928551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928539#post928539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if they ARE 3+, they probably gain the 7+ effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11872-lessens","name":"lessens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T19:50:04-07:00","id":928561,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I was considering an Athletics / Strength Charm that would allow you to inflict knockback on a target equal to the distance you COULD have traveled if you hadn't stopped short to hit someone. Like, if you leaped after someone with Mountain-Crossing Leap technique, but they were only one range band away rather than four.<br /> <br /> Except you really want to use Thunderbolt Attack Prana, Leaping Tiger Attack, or Godspeed Steps for things like that, and...<br /> <br /> TAP and LTA already synergize with Heaven Thunder Hammer in giving that Charm more damage successes or more <i>potential </i>damage successes to fuel its effect. So you can still leap at someone and have the force of that leap magnify your HTH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T21:17:21-07:00","id":928582,"title":"","content":"In light of the discussion, that last is giving me an unfortunately comical mental image.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JuEa6Hum0b4\" data-code=\"JuEa6Hum0b4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/JuEa6Hum0b4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T21:26:35-07:00","id":928584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928366#post928366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, frankly, kind of a ridiculous edge case so unlikely that it should probably be resolved on a table-to-table basis.<br /> <br /> IMHO, I'd say that if you have HTH using this tail slam probably counts as a free activation of it for the purpose of itself or any charms that might stem from it. But I wouldn't let you stack it on top of the extant tail slam.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go with this. It's a ridiculously unlikely edge case, so it should be settled on a case by case basis. &quot;No effect at all&quot; is a bit boring, but it's also the safest way to go. Alternatively you could give some sort of small benefit.<br /> <br /> (I would also want to consider what method the Solar used to turn into that form, and if it's something they're going to be able to do regularly. If it's some sort of bizarre once-in-a-lifetime combination of weird circumstances, or if they've been permanently turned into a stegosaurus with all the attendant disadvantages that implies, I'd be more inclined to let them do slightly ridiculous stuff, whereas if there's a danger of the Solar trying to turn Stegosaurus Slam into their regular fighting style, I would probably want to avoid incentivizing it any more than being a giant dinosaur is already incentivized.)<br /> <br /> This has obvious implications for Lunar charms, although for them it's probably a bit more alright to incentivize turning into a giant dinosaur since it's supposed to be a major part of their fighting style. In that case I would try to make the interactions clear on the charms or give them a general rule for when a Lunar charm overlaps with the native powers of your form. Logically if I'm the Nimble As a Monkey Lunar and I turn into an actual monkey, I should be better at that than a Lunar who hasn't invested in any Nimble As a Monkey charms. Otherwise you end up in a weird place where the Nimble As a Monkey Lunar never wants to turn into an actual monkey due to the redundancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-09-2016, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T22:03:05-07:00","id":928593,"title":"","content":"As solid as your first two paragraphs are, I disagree with your last point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a> - consider, Charms generally cost motes to use; if you can accomplish a similar or even a lesser effect as a monkey for zero motes, it'd be well worthy of a Lunar to at least consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T22:48:12-07:00","id":928604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928593#post928593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As solid as your first two paragraphs are, I disagree with your last point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a> - consider, Charms generally cost motes to use; if you can accomplish a similar or even a lesser effect as a monkey for zero motes, it'd be well worthy of a Lunar to at least consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, sure, but it's still a bit less useful to them than to Lunars who don't have the charms, which is counterintuitive at the very least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T22:49:38-07:00","id":928606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928593#post928593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As solid as your first two paragraphs are, I disagree with your last point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a> - consider, Charms generally cost motes to use; if you can accomplish a similar or even a lesser effect as a monkey for zero motes, it'd be well worthy of a Lunar to at least consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>So an especially agile Lunar becomes no more agile than a not-particularly-agile Lunar when they both turn into monkeys?<br /> <br /> An especially agile Lunar could make a large and clumsy form very agile, potentially more so than a mortal monkey, but cannot be particularly more agile than a mortal monkey as an Exalted monkey?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-09-2016, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T23:43:33-07:00","id":928616,"title":"","content":"If you'd stop trying to twist my words, I'd appreciate it.<br /> <br /> Especially since doing something that monkeys are especially adapted for isn't necessarily a matter of agility. And double especially when this is all hypothetical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T06:45:39-07:00","id":928716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928616#post928616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you'd stop trying to twist my words, I'd appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pointing out the logical conclusions of your proposals is not &quot;twisting&quot; them.<br /> <br /> You were the one who suggested that Lunars could not use agility Charms as monkeys, even when the monkey's abilities would be &quot;a lesser effect&quot;. I pointed out what that would mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T07:07:50-07:00","id":928719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928716#post928716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pointing out the logical conclusions of your proposals is not &quot;twisting&quot; them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please quote the post where I state or even imply something where the &quot;logical conclusion&quot; is\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928606#post928606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An especially agile Lunar could make a large and clumsy form very agile, potentially more so than a mortal monkey\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not the one who started a thread in support of the <i>Gigantobullshit stealthosaurus</i> scene in <i>Jurassic Park</i>, in which a T-rex whose very proximity causes the ground to shake can inexplicably sneak up on humans and intelligent, pack-hunting velociraptors. That was you.<br /> <br /> I am, in fact, <i>rather</i> against being able to use Charms and such in forms where it would be or look utterly ridiculous. I don't want silver houseflies cartoonishly snapping an armored Dynast's neck by slamming into him hard enough. I don't want silver snails easily outpacing a goddamned racehorse. Certain options should, <i>must</i> face the limitations of the form you constrain them in!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-09-2016, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T07:08:36-07:00","id":928720,"title":"","content":"So, if this happened at my table, I would rule that the effect of Heaven Thunder Hammer and Spiked Tail Slam combine to make each range band require 1 less success than normal, and a free knock down even on 0 damage as long as the attack connected. (Maybe 2 successes less if it happened with a really good stunt. But table balance isn't game balance)<br /> <br /> As a general balance thing, for Lunars without an official core book, I'd imagine the effects of animal form can be enhanced with lunar charms, adding bonus effects but it would all need to be written as a case by case basis. Too many things would break if lunar charms and animal effects stacked directly or multiplicative. I don't want a Heaven Spiked Thunder Tail Hammer Slam knock someone around twice doubling all the distances (That with essence 3+ would get even more broken) with twice the dice or twice anything about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4390,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","user":"Deamonlight","date":". 07-09-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:04:44-07:00","id":928752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus#post928258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Siege Lizard, page 572</b><br /> <br /> What happens when the Solar enhances this Brawl attack with the <i>actual</i> Heaven Thunder Hammer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd stack them<br /> <br /> On account of that being mega-cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T09:57:16-07:00","id":928779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928719#post928719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please quote the post where I state or even imply something where the &quot;logical conclusion&quot; is\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928584#post928584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Logically if I'm the Nimble As a Monkey Lunar and I turn into an actual monkey, I should be better at that than a Lunar who hasn't invested in any Nimble As a Monkey charms. Otherwise you end up in a weird place where the Nimble As a Monkey Lunar never wants to turn into an actual monkey due to the redundancy.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928593#post928593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As solid as your first two paragraphs are, I disagree with your last point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a> - consider, Charms generally cost motes to use; if you can accomplish a similar or even a lesser effect as a monkey for zero motes, it'd be well worthy of a Lunar to at least consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was this not a rebuttal of Aquillion's suggestion and a proposal that Lunar Charms should be unable to make a monkey more agile?<br /> <br /> If not, then how did you expect the comment to be taken? No one was going to interpret your comment as a reminder that a Lunar could be more agile just by becoming a monkey and without using Charms, because that's just obvious and it was not the issue being considered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not the one who started a thread in support of the <i>Gigantobullshit stealthosaurus</i> scene in <i>Jurassic Park</i>, in which a T-rex whose very proximity causes the ground to shake can inexplicably sneak up on humans and intelligent, pack-hunting velociraptors. That was you. </div> </div> </div>That was your strawman, you mean.<br /> <br /> The thread was about whether Lunar Exalted in giant forms should be capable of Graceful Crane Stance, while comparing that to the Solar Ability to use Graceful Crane Stance through any mount, including giant animals. It was also about whether it would be cool to have Solars in Warstriders experience a cosmetic semi-failure condition with Graceful Crane Stance and Spider-Foot Method, in regards to walking on water.<br /> <br /> In total, the thread was about &quot;Solars in warstriders and Lunars with shapeshifting can become really big; how should 'graceful' and 'agility' Charms operate in that context?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Support&quot; is also a strong word, given that my stance was &quot;sound/touch-related Stealth as a giant would be nice, and here are some supporting examples&quot;, with an openness to having that be rejected. My stance was not &quot;this is absolutely necessary&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am, in fact, <i>rather</i> against being able to use Charms and such in forms where it would be or look utterly ridiculous. </div> </div> </div>It's awfully curious that you don't want to discuss that in the relevant thread, now isn't it?<br /> <br /> If you have objections and counterarguments, by all means, go post them in the thread that was created for the purpose of having that discussion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want silver houseflies cartoonishly snapping an armored Dynast's neck by slamming into him hard enough. I don't want silver snails easily outpacing a goddamned racehorse. Certain options should, <i>must</i> face the limitations of the form you constrain them in! </div> </div> </div>And THAT sounds like an opinion that belongs in my &quot;Lunars, Size, Strength, and Limitations&quot; thread!<br /> <br /> You just love to drag your disagreements with me out into all the wrong places, don't you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T10:12:08-07:00","id":928791,"title":"","content":"Your failure to understand what is and isn't my position, combined with your smug and baseless taunting, has killed my interest in discussing this further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T11:37:31-07:00","id":928834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928791#post928791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your failure to understand what is and isn't my position, combined with your smug and baseless taunting, has killed my interest in discussing this further.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is probably the wises and most mature response to potential trolling in a thread I've seen on these forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T19:22:51-07:00","id":929018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928791#post928791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your failure to understand what is and isn't my position, combined with your smug and baseless taunting, has killed my interest in discussing this further.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not feeling smug, and rather than taunting you I am challenging your hostility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-09-2016, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T21:20:09-07:00","id":929044,"title":"","content":"Anyway, there are probably ways to finesse it without it being a huge problem. Most of your &quot;nimble as a monkey&quot; charms probably benefit from having high dexterity, which you will in monkey-form. If one or two charms are redundant with your monkey abilities, it isn't the end of the world as long as you have other charms that work well with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am, in fact, <i>rather</i> against being able to use Charms and such in forms where it would be or look utterly ridiculous. I don't want silver houseflies cartoonishly snapping an armored Dynast's neck by slamming into him hard enough. I don't want silver snails easily outpacing a goddamned racehorse. Certain options should, <i>must</i> face the limitations of the form you constrain them in! </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that the charms that care about your attributes would work that way. If you have a charm that does something based on your dexterity, it probably won't work well in snail form.<br /> <br /> But it's not necessarily an either-or thing; there can be some charms that don't care about your form, especially when they're intended to be obviously unnatural. So there might be eg. some Lunar stealth charms that care about your size (or ones intended specifically for when you're tiny), and some that explicitly allow you to ignore it. The Exalted can do impossible things; if a Solar can leap over a mountain, a Lunar can sneak up on them even in the form of a tiger the size of a house. The important thing is doing it when it's cool, which means deciding on a charm-by-charm basis and writing the charms that allow it in a way that sells what you're trying to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T04:46:02-07:00","id":929188,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Alucard, Sunder I'm addressing you both with this because there's clearly a baggage from previous threads clouding this discussion and this isn't the first time something like has happened, is it? So in the words of Queen Elsa, let it go.<br /> Agree to disagree, put each other on ignore I don't care... as long as you find a way forwards. </b></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T12:49:15-07:00","id":929339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=928719#post928719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want silver snails easily outpacing a goddamned racehorse.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If you know you're threadcrapping why do it? Don't do it again. Darksider</span><br /> <br /> .... I kind of think along the lines of Solar's response. Why not? And what actually would be unbalanced if so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-11-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T14:29:08-07:00","id":929388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=929339#post929339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... Do you even weird fantasy bro (your excellency)? I can hear Moebius spinning in his grave...<br /> <br /> (I probably shouldn't response this way to someone who is confirmedly not going to reply ITT, I know).<br /> <br /> .... I kind of think along the lines of Solar's response. Why not? And what actually would be unbalanced if so?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Why do you hate fun/cool/awesome?&quot; is a terrible rebuttal to that statement. Some forms should take a hit to damage; the book agrees, since it has cats doing less damage to larger animals than to ones their size or smaller. You need specific, temporary conditions and magic to get things back up to their nominal levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:10:19-07:00","id":929402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=929388#post929388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Why do you hate fun/cool/awesome?&quot; is a terrible rebuttal to that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, I always hate it when people say that too; but what I am saying is, I think, closer to &quot;This statement is to some degree in specific contradiction to the genres I believe Exalted can/should support&quot; than &quot;When did you decide 'Grinch' was the career path for you?&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T21:08:33-07:00","id":929538,"title":"","content":"The charm Ghost Panther Slinking says this:<br /> <br /> When the Solar controls a familiar using the Sense-Riding<br /> Discipline effect of Spirit-Tied Pet, she can indict the senses<br /> of her enemies. While taking the form of her familiar, the<br /> Exalt may activate any Stealth Charms she knows to protect<br /> her familiar-self from detection.<b>Familiars which are large,<br /> unusual, or otherwise unsuited to stealth may incur penalties<br /> to normal Stealth actions based on unfavorable circumstances\u2014<br /> a claw strider slinking through a forest can<br /> be difficult to notice, but a claw strider skulking through<br /> the shadowed streets of Nexus suffers a -2 penalty.</b><br /> <br /> So going to the absurd, a tyrant lizard has a -3 penalty on stealth rolls but he can still sneak up your ass.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T02:00:16-07:00","id":929620,"title":"","content":"To me it makes way more sense that you'd be able to use any charms which your new form still qualifies for. A snail has no dots in athletics, so no using athletics charms as a snail. A t-rex has insufficient dex to access most of the nice stealth charms, so no using those. As for the original question - If a stegosaurus qualifies, then it should get the full use of any charms the lunar possesses, and as the innate ability isn't Heaven Thunder Hammer, only &quot;like&quot; it, you get to use HTH as well, for much away-going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T02:12:04-07:00","id":929625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/928258-solar-brawler-is-transformed-into-a-stegosaurus?p=929538#post929538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So going to the absurd, a tyrant lizard has a -3 penalty on stealth rolls but he can still sneak up your ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, this would leave it with a Stealth pool of 0, which is pretty reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T02:45:13-07:00","id":929632,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eA7vV4_b9YA\" target=\"_blank\">If this Mosquito doesn't have Ox-Body/Perfect Defenses... I don't know what it does have.</a><br /> <br /> To go from there if someone can functionally use &quot;Magic&quot; to shapeshift and not lose their sense of cognitive functions that let's them do Magic... then by rights they should be able to use their power to further augment their current form. I Admit stealthing as a Tryant lizard would be awkward.. but well. Charms that make you unnoticeable don't care for physics.<br /> <br /> The best answer I've seen to the OP was giving it the Essence 3+ enhancement for having a form that provides a similar effect. Enhancing your form should be possible.. otherwise why even shapeshift for Combat? If your &quot;Better&quot; baseline without making yourself a combat form... then what is the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},